From 3bd8c9165c45045c38bed5a9efa5fe846ab0af50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:40:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Behaviours: version 3 of the data structures of the
 generic-parallel interface

- functions loaded with their `_generic_parallel` suffix (integration,
  initialize functions, post-processings, rotations);
- `mgis_bv_BatchStatistics`: the members of the statistics of the material
  properties (opaque keys of the first failure and of the first unreliable
  result) followed by `rdt`; `mgis_bv_BatchOutputStatus` gives the index
  of the first unreliable result; `statuses` placed after `s1` in
  `mgis_bv_BatchDataView`, as in `TFEL`;
- report function of the library (`<behaviour>_generic_parallel_report`,
  `Behaviour::batch_report`), called by `PendingBatchComputation::getResult`
  instead of decoding the statistics in `MGIS`;
- errors of the batch `-5` (invalid arguments), `-6` (invalid parameters)
  and `-7` (runtime error) reported by exceptions;
- layout checks of all the members copied from `TFEL`, initialization of
  the statistics compared bit for bit with `TFEL`, refusal of the report
  function of a `generic` library.
